{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1624","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Division by Two and Permutation"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an array $$$a$$$ consisting of $$$n$$$ positive integers. You can perform operations on it."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In one operation you can replace any element of the array $$$a_i$$$ with $$$\\lfloor \\frac{a_i}{2} \\rfloor$$$, that is, by an integer part of dividing $$$a_i$$$ by $$$2$$$ (rounding down)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"See if you can apply the operation some number of times (possible $$$0$$$) to make the array $$$a$$$ become a permutation of numbers from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$ —that is, so that it contains all numbers from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$, each exactly once."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, if $$$a = [1, 8, 25, 2]$$$, $$$n = 4$$$, then the answer is yes. You could do the following:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Replace $$$8$$$ with $$$\\lfloor \\frac{8}{2} \\rfloor = 4$$$, then $$$a = [1, 4, 25, 2]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Replace $$$25$$$ with $$$\\lfloor \\frac{25}{2} \\rfloor = 12$$$, then $$$a = [1, 4, 12, 2]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Replace $$$12$$$ with $$$\\lfloor \\frac{12}{2} \\rfloor = 6$$$, then $$$a = [1, 4, 6, 2]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Replace $$$6$$$ with $$$\\lfloor \\frac{6}{2} \\rfloor = 3$$$, then $$$a = [1, 4, 3, 2]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of input data contains an integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$) —the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test case contains exactly two lines. The first one contains an integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 50$$$), the second one contains integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_n$$$ ($$$1 \\le a_i \\le 10^9$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output on a separate line:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if you can make the array $$$a$$$ become a permutation of numbers from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" otherwise. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can output "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in any case (for example, strings "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yEs"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" will be recognized as a positive response)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6\n4\n1 8 25 2\n2\n1 1\n9\n9 8 3 4 2 7 1 5 6\n3\n8 2 1\n4\n24 7 16 7\n5\n22 6 22 4 22\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYES\nNO\nYES\nNO\nNO\nYES\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first test case is explained in the text of the problem statement."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, it is not possible to get a permutation."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"1624C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1624/problem/C"}